module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.GradedAlgebraEpiDegreeOfEpi
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.IdealSheafPowers

/-!
# Multiplication of the Rees algebra of a sheaf of ideals is locally surjective

Let `(C, J, 𝒪)` be a ringed site and let `𝓘 ⊆ 𝒪` be a sheaf of ideals.  Its powers assemble into
the sheaf of graded algebras `⨁_{n ≥ 0} 𝓘ⁿ` of `SheafOfModules.reesGradedAlgebra`.  This file
proves that the multiplication

`𝓘ⁱ ⊗ 𝓘ʲ ⟶ 𝓘^{i + j}`

of that graded algebra, read as a morphism of presheaves of modules out of the objectwise tensor
product, is locally surjective in every pair of nonnegative degrees: **`𝓘^{i + j}` is locally
generated by products of sections of `𝓘ⁱ` and sections of `𝓘ʲ`**.

No hypothesis beyond nonnegativity of the two degrees is needed — in particular no
quasi-coherence, finite type or Noetherian condition.  The reason is that the `n`-th power
`SheafOfModules.idealSheafPow` is *defined* by the covering sieve `SheafOfModules.powSieve`:  a
local section of `𝓘^{i + j}` over an object is, by definition, a section of `𝒪` which on a
covering sieve restricts into the `(i + j)`-st power of the *ideal of sections*.  Over each arrow
of that sieve `Submodule.pow_add` writes the restriction as a finite sum of products of a section
of the `i`-th power and a section of the `j`-th power of the ideal of sections, and each factor of
each product is a fortiori a section of the corresponding power of the sheaf of ideals.  So the
sieve witnessing membership in `𝓘^{i + j}` already witnesses local surjectivity, and no further
covering is taken.

The degrees have to be nonnegative: `SheafOfModules.idealSheafZPow` is the zero sheaf of ideals in
negative degrees, so for `i < 0` the source of the multiplication is the zero presheaf while its
target `𝓘^{i + j}` need not be.

## Main definitions

* `SheafOfModules.reesMulPresheaf`: multiplication of the Rees graded algebra in a fixed pair of
  degrees, as a morphism of presheaves of modules out of the objectwise tensor product.

## Main results

* `SheafOfModules.isLocallySurjective_reesMulPresheaf`: **multiplication of the Rees graded
  algebra of a sheaf of ideals is locally surjective in every pair of nonnegative degrees.**
* `SheafOfModules.epi_unitalHom_app_add_reesGradedAlgebra`: consequently a unital homomorphism
  into the Rees graded algebra which is an isomorphism in two nonnegative degrees is an
  epimorphism in their sum.  This is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.epi_unitalHom_app_add` with its
  local-surjectivity hypothesis discharged, and it is the degree-propagation step for the whole
  family of Rees algebras.

## Implementation notes

The ring of sections of the structure sheaf of a ringed site is commutative, which is what
`SheafOfModules.reesGradedAlgebra` takes as its `hcomm` argument;
`SheafOfModules.mul_comm_of_ringedSite` records it so that the Rees algebra of a sheaf of ideals
on a ringed site can be named without repeating the proof.  It generalises
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.mul_comm_structureSheaf`, which states the same thing for the objects of
the site of opens of a topological space; that lemma is not usable for an arbitrary site, and the
two should be merged onto this one when `StacksFrontier/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/
SheafHomSlice.lean` is next edited.

`Submodule.pow_add` requires its second exponent to be nonzero, so the degenerate degree is
handled separately: there the single product `x = x · 1` already exhibits the section, the second
factor being the unit section, which lies in the zeroth power.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FQW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FQW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01AH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01AH)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

open scoped TensorProduct

universe v u w

namespace SheafOfModules

open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification (structureRingPresheaf structureSheaf)

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {O : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{w}}
  (hO : Presheaf.IsSheaf J (structureRingPresheaf O))

/-- **The ring of sections of the structure sheaf of a ringed site is commutative.**  This is the
`hcomm` argument of `SheafOfModules.reesGradedAlgebra` for the structure sheaf of a ringed
site. -/
theorem mul_comm_of_ringedSite (X : Cᵒᵖ)
    (a b : ToType ((structureSheaf O hO).obj.obj X)) : a * b = b * a :=
  mul_comm (G := ToType ((O ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w}).obj X)) a b

variable (I : (unit (structureSheaf O hO)).Submodule)

/-- **The Rees graded algebra `⨁_{n ≥ 0} 𝓘ⁿ` of a sheaf of ideals on a ringed site.** -/
noncomputable def reesGradedAlgebraOfRingedSite : GradedAlgebra.{w, w} (structureSheaf O hO) :=
  reesGradedAlgebra I (mul_comm_of_ringedSite hO)

theorem reesGradedAlgebraOfRingedSite_piece (n : ℤ) :
    (reesGradedAlgebraOfRingedSite hO I).piece n = reesPiece I n :=
  rfl

/-- **Multiplication of the Rees graded algebra in the degrees `i` and `j`**, as a morphism of
presheaves of modules out of the objectwise tensor product.  This is the shape in which
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.epi_unitalHom_app_add` consumes the multiplication of its target. -/
noncomputable def reesMulPresheaf (i j : ℤ) :
    PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (reesPiece I i).val (reesPiece I j).val ⟶
      (reesPiece I (i + j)).val :=
  PresheafOfModules.ofBilinear (reesMul I (mul_comm_of_ringedSite hO) i j)

/-- Multiplication of the Rees graded algebra carries the pure tensor of two homogeneous local
sections to their product. -/
theorem reesMulPresheaf_tmul (i j : ℤ) (X : Cᵒᵖ) (x : (reesPiece I i).val.obj X)
    (y : (reesPiece I j).val.obj X) :
    PresheafOfModules.Hom.app (reesMulPresheaf hO I i j) X (x ⊗ₜ[O.obj X] y) =
      ((reesGradedAlgebraOfRingedSite hO I).mul i j).app X x y :=
  PresheafOfModules.ofBilinear_tmul _ X x y

theorem reesVal_reesMulPresheaf_tmul (i j : ℤ) (X : Cᵒᵖ) (x : (reesPiece I i).val.obj X)
    (y : (reesPiece I j).val.obj X) :
    reesVal I (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app (reesMulPresheaf hO I i j) X (x ⊗ₜ[O.obj X] y)) =
      reesVal I x * reesVal I y := by
  rw [reesMulPresheaf_tmul]
  rfl

/-- The property of a section of the structure sheaf of being the product of two homogeneous
local sections of the degrees `i` and `j`, up to a finite sum. -/
private def IsReesProduct (i j : ℤ) {X : Cᵒᵖ} (x : ToType ((structureSheaf O hO).obj.obj X)) :
    Prop :=
  ∃ t : (PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (reesPiece I i).val (reesPiece I j).val).obj X,
    reesVal I (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app (reesMulPresheaf hO I i j) X t) = x

/-- Membership in the integer-indexed power at a natural exponent is membership in the natural
power. -/
private theorem mem_idealAt_idealSheafZPow_natCast {n : ℕ} {X : Cᵒᵖ}
    {x : ToType ((structureSheaf O hO).obj.obj X)} :
    x ∈ idealAt (idealSheafZPow I (n : ℤ)) X ↔ x ∈ idealAt (idealSheafPow I n) X := by
  rw [idealSheafZPow_natCast]

/-- A product of a section of the `a`-th power of the ideal of sections and a section of the
`b`-th power is the image of a pure tensor. -/
private theorem isReesProduct_mul {a b : ℕ} {X : Cᵒᵖ}
    {x y : ToType ((structureSheaf O hO).obj.obj X)}
    (hx : x ∈ idealAt I X ^ a) (hy : y ∈ idealAt I X ^ b) :
    IsReesProduct hO I (a : ℤ) (b : ℤ) (x * y) :=
  ⟨reesMk I (n := (a : ℤ)) x ((mem_idealAt_idealSheafZPow_natCast hO I).2
      (mem_idealSheafPow_of_mem_pow I a hx)) ⊗ₜ[O.obj X]
      reesMk I (n := (b : ℤ)) y ((mem_idealAt_idealSheafZPow_natCast hO I).2
      (mem_idealSheafPow_of_mem_pow I b hy)),
    reesVal_reesMulPresheaf_tmul hO I _ _ X _ _⟩

/-- **A section of the `(a + b)`-th power of the ideal of sections is a finite sum of products of
a section of the `a`-th power and a section of the `b`-th power.** -/
private theorem isReesProduct_of_mem_pow_add (a b : ℕ) {X : Cᵒᵖ}
    {x : ToType ((structureSheaf O hO).obj.obj X)} (hx : x ∈ idealAt I X ^ (a + b)) :
    IsReesProduct hO I (a : ℤ) (b : ℤ) x := by
  rcases eq_or_ne b 0 with hb | hb
  · have hx' : x ∈ idealAt I X ^ a := by rwa [hb, Nat.add_zero] at hx
    have hone : (1 : ToType ((structureSheaf O hO).obj.obj X)) ∈ idealAt I X ^ b := by
      rw [hb, Submodule.pow_zero, Ideal.one_eq_top]
      exact Submodule.mem_top
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := isReesProduct_mul hO I hx' hone
    exact ⟨t, ht.trans (mul_one x)⟩
  · rw [Submodule.pow_add _ hb] at hx
    refine Submodule.mul_induction_on hx (fun p hp q hq => isReesProduct_mul hO I hp hq) ?_
    rintro y z ⟨t, ht⟩ ⟨t', ht'⟩
    refine ⟨t + t', ?_⟩
    rw [map_add, reesVal_add, ht, ht']

/-- **Multiplication of the Rees graded algebra of a sheaf of ideals is locally surjective in
every pair of nonnegative degrees**: a local section of `𝓘^{i + j}` is, on a covering sieve, a
finite sum of products of a section of `𝓘ⁱ` and a section of `𝓘ʲ`.

The covering sieve is the one witnessing membership in `𝓘^{i + j}`, which by the definition of
`SheafOfModules.idealSheafPow` restricts the section into the `(i + j)`-st power of the ideal of
sections; `Submodule.pow_add` splits that into products over each arrow of the sieve. -/
theorem isLocallySurjective_reesMulPresheaf (a b : ℕ) :
    PresheafOfModules.IsLocallySurjective J (reesMulPresheaf hO I (a : ℤ) (b : ℤ)) := by
  constructor
  intro U s
  have hs : reesVal I s ∈ idealAt (idealSheafPow I (a + b)) (op U) :=
    (mem_idealAt_idealSheafZPow_natCast hO I).1 (by exact_mod_cast reesVal_mem I s)
  refine J.superset_covering (fun W f hf => ?_) ((mem_idealSheafPow_iff I (a + b) _).1 hs)
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := isReesProduct_of_mem_pow_add hO I a b hf
  exact ⟨t, reesPiece_ext I ht⟩

/-- **A unital homomorphism of sheaves of graded algebras into the Rees graded algebra of a sheaf
of ideals which is an isomorphism in two nonnegative degrees is an epimorphism in their sum.**
This is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.epi_unitalHom_app_add` with its local-surjectivity hypothesis
discharged by `SheafOfModules.isLocallySurjective_reesMulPresheaf`. -/
theorem epi_unitalHom_app_add_reesGradedAlgebra
    {A : GradedAlgebra.{w, w} (structureSheaf O hO)}
    (φ : GradedAlgebra.UnitalHom A (reesGradedAlgebraOfRingedSite hO I)) (a b : ℕ)
    (ha : IsIso (φ.app (a : ℤ))) (hb : IsIso (φ.app (b : ℤ))) :
    Epi (φ.app ((a : ℤ) + (b : ℤ))) :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.epi_unitalHom_app_add (O := O) (hO := hO) φ (a : ℤ) (b : ℤ) ha hb
    (reesMulPresheaf hO I (a : ℤ) (b : ℤ)) (reesMulPresheaf_tmul hO I (a : ℤ) (b : ℤ))
    (isLocallySurjective_reesMulPresheaf hO I a b)

/-- **Multiplication of the Rees graded algebra of a sheaf of ideals is locally surjective in
every pair of nonnegative degrees**, with the degrees written as integers. -/
theorem isLocallySurjective_reesMulPresheaf_of_nonneg {i j : ℤ} (hi : 0 ≤ i) (hj : 0 ≤ j) :
    PresheafOfModules.IsLocallySurjective J (reesMulPresheaf hO I i j) := by
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ : ∃ a : ℕ, i = (a : ℤ) := ⟨i.toNat, (Int.toNat_of_nonneg hi).symm⟩
  obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ : ∃ b : ℕ, j = (b : ℤ) := ⟨j.toNat, (Int.toNat_of_nonneg hj).symm⟩
  exact isLocallySurjective_reesMulPresheaf hO I a b

/-! ### Propagation of surjectivity and invertibility to every nonnegative degree -/

section Propagation

variable [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  {A : GradedAlgebra.{w, w} (structureSheaf O hO)}

/-- **A unital homomorphism into the Rees graded algebra of a sheaf of ideals which is surjective
in two nonnegative degrees is surjective in their sum.** -/
theorem epi_unitalHom_app_add_reesGradedAlgebra_of_epi
    (φ : GradedAlgebra.UnitalHom A (reesGradedAlgebraOfRingedSite hO I)) {i j : ℤ}
    (hi : 0 ≤ i) (hj : 0 ≤ j) (hei : Epi (φ.app i)) (hej : Epi (φ.app j)) :
    Epi (φ.app (i + j)) :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.epi_unitalHom_app_add_of_epi (O := O) (hO := hO) φ i j hei hej
    (reesMulPresheaf hO I i j) (reesMulPresheaf_tmul hO I i j)
    (isLocallySurjective_reesMulPresheaf_of_nonneg hO I hi hj)

/-- **A unital homomorphism into the Rees graded algebra of a sheaf of ideals which is surjective
in the degrees zero and one is surjective in every nonnegative degree.**

This is the degree induction: the step from `n` to `n + 1` multiplies by a degree-one section,
and `SheafOfModules.isLocallySurjective_reesMulPresheaf` says that every local section of
`𝓘^{n + 1}` is locally a sum of such products. -/
theorem epi_unitalHom_app_of_nonneg
    (φ : GradedAlgebra.UnitalHom A (reesGradedAlgebraOfRingedSite hO I))
    (h0 : Epi (φ.app 0)) (h1 : Epi (φ.app 1)) : ∀ n : ℤ, 0 ≤ n → Epi (φ.app n) :=
  Int.leInduction h0 (fun _n hn hen =>
    epi_unitalHom_app_add_reesGradedAlgebra_of_epi hO I φ hn zero_le_one hen h1)

/-- **A unital homomorphism into the Rees graded algebra of a sheaf of ideals which is invertible
in the degrees zero and one and injective in every nonnegative degree is invertible in every
nonnegative degree.**

Only surjectivity of the two input degrees is used: it propagates to every nonnegative degree by
`SheafOfModules.epi_unitalHom_app_of_nonneg`, and injectivity in the degree in question then
upgrades the epimorphism to an isomorphism, the category of sheaves of modules being balanced.
Injectivity is a hypothesis: nothing about a Rees algebra makes a surjection in degrees zero and
one injective in higher degrees. -/
theorem isIso_unitalHom_app_of_nonneg (hbal : Balanced (_root_.SheafOfModules.{w}
      (structureSheaf O hO)))
    (φ : GradedAlgebra.UnitalHom A (reesGradedAlgebraOfRingedSite hO I))
    (h0 : IsIso (φ.app 0)) (h1 : IsIso (φ.app 1))
    (hmono : ∀ n : ℤ, 0 ≤ n → Mono (φ.app n)) (n : ℤ) (hn : 0 ≤ n) : IsIso (φ.app n) :=
  @isIso_of_mono_of_epi _ _ hbal _ _ _ (hmono n hn)
    (epi_unitalHom_app_of_nonneg hO I φ (@IsIso.epi_of_iso _ _ _ _ _ h0)
      (@IsIso.epi_of_iso _ _ _ _ _ h1) n hn)

end Propagation

end SheafOfModules

end
